1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,612
Welcome to Keepsake.

2
00:00:01,612 --> 00:00:08,587
This is the Woodland Writing Room: a quiet place to collect photos, make scrapbooks,
and revisit small memories.

3
00:00:08,587 --> 00:00:12,462
Move between the writing desk, reading corner, and memory wall.

4
00:00:15,450 --> 00:00:17,817
Room settings bring the atmosphere together.

5
00:00:17,817 --> 00:00:23,339
Choose daylight, dusk, or nighttime, change the season and weather, and control
individual lights.

6
00:00:23,339 --> 00:00:28,467
Balanced and High graphics are saved preferences for the person using the room.

7
00:00:30,450 --> 00:00:32,861
Open the book on your desk to begin.

8
00:00:32,861 --> 00:00:36,476
Cover and title lets you name the scrapbook and choose its appearance.

9
00:00:36,476 --> 00:00:41,297
Turn through your memories with the page arrows, or use the page overview to jump
ahead.

10
00:00:45,450 --> 00:00:50,803
Add photos from your computer or phone, or choose memories already in the filing
cabinet.

11
00:00:50,803 --> 00:00:54,372
A batch can hold twenty photos, arranged four per page.

12
00:00:54,372 --> 00:00:58,297
Folder uploads in the cabinet create a category you can name.

13
00:01:00,450 --> 00:01:03,901
Add a handwritten touch with the markers, including blue.

14
00:01:03,901 --> 00:01:08,502
Adjust the line thickness beside them, then draw directly on the page.

15
00:01:08,502 --> 00:01:13,487
Stickers, captions, and the bottom toolbar help you arrange and refine the
composition.

16
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:19,009
Your saved scrapbooks live on the upper shelf with readable titles.

17
00:01:19,009 --> 00:01:23,539
Hover over a spine to tilt the book outward, then select it to open.

18
00:01:23,539 --> 00:01:27,422
The blank book starts a new scrapbook, which becomes your desk book.

19
00:01:30,450 --> 00:01:33,438
The mini photo printer gives a memory a physical moment.

20
00:01:33,438 --> 00:01:35,529
Choose a photograph and watch it emerge.

21
00:01:35,529 --> 00:01:40,907
Then send the print to a scrapbook, or take it to the map and choose where it
belongs.

22
00:01:45,450 --> 00:01:50,930
With the owner’s permission, friends can view shared scrapbooks and leave a twenty
character sticky note.

23
00:01:50,930 --> 00:01:53,328
Notes on and off controls their visibility.

24
00:01:53,328 --> 00:01:54,698
New notes await approval.

25
00:01:54,698 --> 00:01:59,150
This demonstration uses the local friend preview; online visits are still to come.

26
00:02:00,450 --> 00:02:05,090
Music settings let you choose a quiet entrance or a configured music selection.

27
00:02:05,090 --> 00:02:07,946
Spotify and SoundCloud have their own setup controls.

28
00:02:07,946 --> 00:02:13,657
Choose a CRT screen color to match your mood, and adjust music and room sound
levels.

29
00:02:15,450 --> 00:02:18,875
Open the desk drawer to browse the mini shop.

30
00:02:18,875 --> 00:02:23,822
Its four categories hold sticker packs, windowsill decorations, room variants, and
creative extras.

31
00:02:23,822 --> 00:02:29,150
The prototype uses collectible stamps, with room and item availability shown before
you choose.

32
00:02:30,450 --> 00:02:36,706
The guestbook collects a quiet hello from a visitor, with an option to request a
copy on the desk.

33
00:02:36,706 --> 00:02:39,340
Little discoveries add occasional notes around the room.

34
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:42,632
Their frequency and desk note preference are yours to control.

35
00:02:45,450 --> 00:02:47,505
Your changes save in this browser.

36
00:02:47,505 --> 00:02:52,300
Saving and storage shows the current status and lets you download a room backup.

37
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:55,382
Keep one before changing devices or clearing browser data.

38
00:02:55,382 --> 00:02:59,150
That is Woodland: a small room that grows with your memories.
